Sugar And Our Kids[: Are We] Doing Enough[?]
When my son eats[ a major] sugar bomb,[ like a piece of] cake at a birthday party,[ I] can see[ his] mood change. His[ generally sweet] and[ cooperative] disposition shifts to one of[ a fired up wild] child[,] which is soon followed[ by a] crash of energy and crankiness. His ability to follow directions, typically a positive trait for my son,[ w]anes as a result as well.[
]Watching[ this] outwardly behavioral[ roller] coaster is[ like tracing] the steps[ of] sugar’[s] overt and[ undeniable] physiological impact on my son. The sugar is[ sending] signals and triggering reactions in his young and[ developing] mind and body.

